cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenEchelon: a model-agnostic runtime for structured AI organizations"
message: "If you reference OpenEchelon in academic or technical work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OpenEchelon Contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/NAME0x0/OpenEchelon"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NAME0x0/OpenEchelon"
url: "https://github.com/NAME0x0/OpenEchelon"
abstract: >-
  OpenEchelon is an open-source runtime for building hierarchical organizations
  of AI agents. Rather than a flat multi-agent swarm, it models an organization
  with a CEO, executives, directors, managers, specialists, and workers, each
  holding defined authority, permissions, memory, reasoning budgets, and
  reporting lines. Agent identity is separate from model execution, so the same
  logical employee may be executed by a local model, a frontier API, or a CLI
  coding agent depending on task difficulty and available quota. A Resource
  Governor routes work to the cheapest intelligence that can complete it
  reliably. The human owner retains final authority over the organization.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - multi-agent-systems
  - agent-orchestration
  - agentic-ai
  - llm-orchestration
  - hierarchical-agents
  - model-agnostic
